.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH scanr 1  "scanr 0.5.0" 
.SH NAME
scanr \- Proxy\-aware TCP connect scanner with reproducible, durable scan records
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscanr\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
scanr performs unprivileged TCP connect() probes directly or through a SOCKS5 or HTTP CONNECT proxy, streams open ports to stdout as they are found, and always writes a JSONL record containing the fully resolved configuration and a single terminal event stating whether the run completed, was interrupted, or failed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Use this config file instead of the discovered user and project files
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress the header, progress, and summary on stderr
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show additional detail
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable coloured output (also honours NO_COLOR)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
scanr\-run(1)
Execute a scan
.TP
scanr\-plan(1)
Resolve a scan and show the plan without touching the network
.TP
scanr\-config(1)
Inspect and manage configuration
.TP
scanr\-transport(1)
Inspect and test transports
.TP
scanr\-output(1)
Inspect prior scan records
.TP
scanr\-completion(1)
Generate a shell completion script
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  scanr config init
  scanr plan internal\-web
  scanr run internal\-web
  scanr run internal\-web \-\-profile proxy\-careful
  scanr run \-\-targets 10.20.30.0/24 \-\-ports 22,80,443
  subfinder \-d example.com | scanr run \-\-targets \- \-\-ports web
  scanr transport test lab
  scanr output verify scanr\-results/scan\-*.jsonl.gz
.SH VERSION
v0.5.0
